=== knowledgeable_talk ===
He laughs. "That's what happens when you pay attention. Most people here are too busy performing to actually observe."
+ [...]
- "Take Gaten, for instance—he's been checking Alistair's favorite sitting area every ten minutes like he's expecting a report card. The man can't function without approval."
+ [...]
- "Brooklyn's the opposite—she's been holding court like she already wears the crown. Bold move for someone in her position. Then again, desperation makes people bold, doesn't it?"
    -> choice_menu

=== unusual_talk ===
"Unusual? At a masquerade ball?" He grins. "Everything's unusual. But if you're asking if I've noticed the tension..."
+ [...]
- "Derek nearly crushed a wine glass when someone mentioned military appointments. Flora's been avoiding Alistair's like he's the plague."
+ [...]
- "And I could swear I saw Estelle crying near the discussion room’s entrance earlier. Poor thing looked terrified."
+ [...]
- He shrugs. "But servants always have their dramas, don't they? Not really our concern."
    -> choice_menu

=== calm_talk ===
"Why wouldn't I be calm? I've learned everything I know from the best. Alistair taught me that power is a game of chess, not checkers."
+ [...]
- "You stay three moves ahead, you keep your mask on, and you never, ever let them see you sweat." 
+ [...]
- adjusts his silver cufflinks Alistair taught me everything... perhaps too well. A student eventually surpasses the teacher, don't you think?"
+ [...]
- "Speaking of which, have you met dear Alistair yet? No? Well, he's probably in one of his 'discussions.' The man does love his private negotiations."
